# Persistent skeletal mesh section authoring — 2026-09-21

## Scope and API basis

Added `UUnrealMCPSkeletalMeshEditorSubsystem` to the existing editor-only
UnrealMCP module. Python can query sections and persist the mesh editor's
section enabled/disabled state through the existing generic Python bridge.
No bridge registration, project C++, module descriptor, or existing dirty source
file was modified. Usage is in `Docs/Tools/skeletal_tools.md`.

UE 5.6.1's `SkeletalMeshEditorSubsystem` does not expose this setter. The native
implementation follows `PersonaMeshDetails::OnSectionEnabledChanged`: suspend
alternate skin-weight preview, scope PostEditChange, transact/Modify/PreEditChange,
set the parent and bone-limit chunks, update source section user data, then
rebuild. The target mesh's initial async compilation is finished before reading
its imported model. No old section reference is used after rebuild.

